  "failed_attempts": [
    "The initial regression fails because the follower has no accepted-store refresh schedule.",
    "The first implementation run fails its five-second adoption wait. Its log records cancellation during cleanup. Later runs remove duplicate decoding and allow 30 seconds for fixture processing. This wait is not a product latency target.",
    "Global golangci-lint 2.13.1 reports two findings in unchanged native observer code. Pinned 2.12.2 initially panics while it reads Go 1.27 sources. Pinned 2.12.2 with GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.6 passes.",
    "The first prose check reports two source-comment diagnostics. The final edit changes those comments only, and all 1,511 files pass.",
    "The first canonical documentation check reports one seven-sentence paragraph. A paragraph split fixes it, and the final 1,322-file prose check passes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Focused component evidence only. Full delivery verification, review, native integration, publication, and merge remain required.",
    "The takeover tests use an in-memory catalog store and a stub lease. They prove the running-follower input guard, not a complete fleet backend.",
    "Cold restart eligibility, shared retained-input recovery, equivalent acquisition capability, and atomic lease/head fencing remain unqualified. CSP11 owns full fleet recovery and fencing.",
    "Explicit authority transitions and Starport production clock composition remain incomplete.",
    "Both Windows native jobs still fail at PR #151 head a6545493. Linux and macOS jobs pass. No Windows gate is waived.",
    "Two source comments changed after the race checks. No executable Go statement changed after those checks."
  ],
